From 9876fefc3ce88d875aaf97571fe2e008c0590d8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:03:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] FBar kernels: tangent by kernels without gradients by kernels
 refused at setup

The stiffness matrices of a behaviour integrator depending on the current
estimate of the solution (FBar formulation) are computed by kernels from
data computed with the gradients by kernels: the setup of the resolution
now refuses the stiffness matrices computed by kernels, assembled or
applied without assembly, with gradients computed element by element
(`MultiMaterialNonLinearIntegrator::checkStiffnessMatricesKernelsSupport`),
instead of a failure of the first assembly, seen as a failure of the
convergence. The validity of the data is kept as a safeguard, checked
before the tangent operator already computed, which is discarded with the
data.

Other changes: documentation of `TangentOperatorComputation`, the vector
`b` written by the kernel computing it, names of the functions passed as C
strings, refusal tested with a tangent operator applied without assembly,
prediction in the FBar case with quadratic elements.
